1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,927
An offline-first teacher tool for rural primary schools. Parents use ordinary SMS. Pupils have no account or app.

2
00:00:14,927 --> 00:00:27,635
English, Hausa, Yoruba or Igbo. Non-English interface strings are drafts and fall back to English until native review.

3
00:00:27,635 --> 00:00:38,238
Cloud sync and live SMS are not connected. The preview runs on synthetic data only.

4
00:00:38,238 --> 00:00:45,951
Today's classes, pending sync, parent messages and quick actions in one calm dashboard.

5
00:00:45,951 --> 00:00:53,250
A teacher can manage multiple classes, open a roster and add a pupil locally.

6
00:00:53,250 --> 00:01:07,762
Only absent pupils create an immediate notification job after server acceptance. Present and late do not.

7
00:01:07,762 --> 00:01:17,620
A saved 5E lesson is a teacher-authored scaffold, not a claim of full NERDC coverage.

8
00:01:17,620 --> 00:01:35,307
On-device Gemini Nano is unavailable on this emulator. Curated teaching strategies work offline; cloud AI is not configured.

9
00:01:35,307 --> 00:01:45,555
In this preview the SMS adapter is mocked, so nothing leaves the device.

10
00:01:45,555 --> 00:01:55,078
A teacher replies from Tiny. Provider acceptance is not the same as delivery.

11
00:01:55,078 --> 00:02:07,146
The Note 10 plus is a general test device. Gemini Nano requires supported physical hardware.

12
00:02:07,146 --> 00:02:26,218
Remaining gates: Firebase access, App Distribution, native translation review and a supported on-device AI device.
